=== PARITY (vs web VehicleSpecsWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (VehicleSpecsSource -> VehicleSpecsModel):
    useVehicles, useVehicleSpecs, useVehicleOptions, useVehicleConfigLatest, useTranslation. The production app
    wires VehicleSpecsSource over the shared Vehicles store (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<...>>); the view
    performs NO HTTP. The web's `isLoading/isFetching/isStale/isError` combine across the three queries -> the
    seam pushes a single merged status + connection per snapshot.
  Projection -> VehicleSpecsProjectionBuilder is a faithful port of the web `entries` useMemo + compact derivation:
      * asString(unknown) — non-empty strings pass / numbers stringify / else nil (web asString).
      * 7 fixed rows in web order: Model (car_type ?? model ?? config.car_type), Trim (trim_badging ?? trim ??
        config.trim), Paint Color (exterior_color ?? config.exterior_color), Wheels (wheel_type ??
        config.wheel_type), Interior (interior ?? interior_color), Aux Battery (aux_battery_type), Car Version
        (config.version ?? car_version, MONO). Each missing value -> "—".
      * Options: decoded option codes -> neutral-badge rows, value = asString(options[key]) ?? key, capped at 8
        (web slice(0,8)). Swift dicts are unordered, so keys are SORTED for a deterministic, stable projection
        (documented platform-necessary adaptation of web Object.keys insertion order).
      * hasData = specs != nil || options != nil || config != nil (web hasAnyData) -> drives content vs empty.
    Verified by the EXECUTED XCTest adapter suite (10 cases) under real Xcode — see gate steps [1]/[2].
  Composition -> WidgetShell chrome (doc.text icon + "Vehicle Specs" title + freshness chip + refresh + Open) ·
    compact (cols<=1): doc.text glyph + model headline + "Trim: {trim}" · standard (2x4): WidgetDetailCard list —
    one row per spec (label · value · optional neutral option badge) + dividers, in a ScrollView.
  Shared components -> @/components/feedback -> ContentUnavailableView (EmptyState), @/components/motion (FadeIn)
    -> native content transition. Reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSSkeleton / TSTone compiled
    against the REAL apps/apple tokens + components in the build below. Recharts->none / Leaflet->none.
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No specs available") · error (retry) ·
    stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached value + chip + banner) · content (compact + standard). Model phase
    resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell.
